# C1 end: the Shatter. The last scene of Chapter 1.
# Kaelen and Elara come through onto the Ironhold side, see the city, look back
# at Oakhaven (Aldric first, then the village meeting), and turn toward Ironhold.
# Replaces the inline lines of play_bridge_approach(), play_environmental_shift(),
# play_the_shatter() and play_post_shatter_dialogue() in
# scripts/chapter1/ch1_shatter_transition.gd.
# Elara is always with Kaelen here (elara_meeting.dlg keeps her in every branch),
# so there is no solo branch. She uses his name.
# It's night: Tobb is asleep (fragment_one.dlg) and after_kill says "It's not morning".
#
# Nodes the scene runs one at a time, between its own effects, in this order:
#   bridge       Kaelen and Elara walk onto the bridge (after they enter, before mid-bridge).
#   shift        the colour drains and the boundary starts to go.
#   reconstruct  one System line while the screen is black, after the break.
#   start        post-shatter entry (everything from here on runs as one dialogue).
# Nothing before the break mentions weight; "start" opens on it.
#
# Scene events (the scene implements these):
#   do desaturate     start the colour drain. NEW. Must land before Kaelen's grey-lamps line.
#   do shake          short camera shake. NEW. Must land before "The bridge is still here."
#   do pan_ironhold   camera pans over the city; hide the dialogue box.
#   do look_back      Kaelen turns toward Oakhaven. Once per path, in the Aldric node.
#   do pause 2.0      built in.
#
# Flag order (reads flags only; sets none):
#   1. Aldric, router "aldric": ch1_root_purge, then ch1_knight_killed, then
#      ch1_knight_spared, else after_none.
#      Purge also sets ch1_knight_spared (aldric.dlg), so it is checked first.
#      A kill also reads ch1_aldric_kill_owned / _justified / _unsure.
#      A save with no Aldric flag (made before the rewrite) gets after_none.
#   2. Village meeting, router "village": ch1_oakhaven_warned_villagers, then
#      ch1_oakhaven_warned_leaders, then ch1_oakhaven_left_quietly, else
#      village_none. fragment_one.dlg sets exactly one, so the order only matters
#      for old or broken saves.

# ── Before the break ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

~ bridge
Kaelen: Halfway across, the oak stops and it's steel the rest of the way, riveted down in rows. I've been counting the rivets.
Elara: Oakhaven ends where the oak does. Mind the seam between the two; it's caught better boots than yours.
Kaelen (Internal): Somebody chose where that seam goes. Nothing that grows or rusts ends this straight on its own.
Elara: Stay on the middle planks. If I say walk, you walk, and you don't stop to look at anything.
Kaelen: It's a bridge. People cross bridges every day, and almost none of them— middle planks. Got it.
=> END

~ shift
do desaturate
Kaelen: The lamps back in Oakhaven were yellow a second ago, and now they're grey. So's your cloak. So are my hands.
System: SYSTEM TRACE: REGION BOUNDARY — OAKHAVEN REACH / IRONHOLD CROWN.
Elara: Here it comes. Feel that? Warm as Mara's back step on baking day. That's the other side, and we don't stop for it.
Kaelen: It's not only warm. There's a hum under the planks, like a transformer in the minute before it—
do shake
Kaelen: The bridge is still here. You're still here. Please, both of you, stay that way.
Elara: Then walk. Eyes on my back, not the river, and not on Oakhaven either.
=> END

# The screen is black. The world speaking, not a greeting.
~ reconstruct
System: SYSTEM TRACE: RECONSTRUCTION COMPLETE. REGION: IRONHOLD CROWN.
=> END

# ── After the break ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

~ start
Kaelen (Internal): Everything's heavier. My boots, my arms, the sword. Like the ground just remembered I'm standing on it.
Kaelen: Two possibilities. The whole world just came apart and rebuilt itself around us, or I hit my head on the rail and I'm—
Elara: You didn't hit your head. I was watching it the whole way over.
Elara: First time I came this way, I lost an hour and my breakfast in a ditch. You're still standing, which is more than I managed.
Kaelen (Internal): The air tastes like soot and hot copper, and there's steam hissing somewhere close that never stops for breath.
do pan_ironhold
Kaelen: All those chimneys. That's Ironhold, isn't it? What are we walking into?
Elara: Work, mostly. Forges, caravan yards, a bell for every shift. And a gate that asks who you are, so think of something.
Kaelen: I've got a name. Past that, I've got a flight number and a sword that isn't mine.
=> aldric

~ aldric
[if ch1_root_purge] => after_purge
[if ch1_knight_killed] => after_kill
[if ch1_knight_spared] => after_spare
=> after_none

~ after_kill
do look_back
Kaelen (Internal): Somewhere behind that smoke is the gate he died guarding. From here I could cover it with my thumb.
Elara: You've stopped walking again. That's twice since the bridge.
Kaelen: He said "good". Right before. Just the one word, and I keep turning it over like there's a—
Elara: He meant it. Aldric never said anything he didn't mean, not even to be kind.
[if ch1_aldric_kill_owned] Kaelen: You told me not to dress it up. I killed him. That's the whole of it, and I'm not adding anything.
[if ch1_aldric_kill_justified] Kaelen: He was a threat. That's true. I just thought true would weigh more than this.
[if ch1_aldric_kill_unsure] Kaelen: You said it'd still be there in the morning. It's not morning yet, and it hasn't moved an inch.
Elara: Then carry it, and pass some over when it gets too heavy. I've hauled worse than you up worse hills.
=> village

~ after_spare
do look_back
Kaelen (Internal): He's back there in his own village, still arguing with an order nobody else can hear.
Elara: He'll come back or he won't. Staring at the smoke won't tip it, and we're losing the dark.
Kaelen: One more second. I want to be the last one who looked.
Elara: Mara will feed him and Bran will write down every time he sneezes. He won't get a minute to himself.
Kaelen: If he's still in there, the directive slips eventually. It has to. And if he isn't—
Elara: Don't finish that. Not this close to home.
=> village

~ after_purge
do look_back
Kaelen (Internal): He knew her name. He knew she was lying. Two things the purge didn't take, and I can't count the ones it did.
Elara: He knew me. Called me a liar, same as ever. I keep waiting to find out what he's lost instead.
Kaelen: I'm sorry, I— I didn't know what it would cost, and I did it anyway. I should have—
Elara: You told me you didn't know, before you did it, not after. I'll keep that part.
Kaelen: And the rest of it?
Elara: Ask me in a week. Ask him, if he's the one who answers.
=> village

~ after_none
do look_back
Kaelen (Internal): Oakhaven's behind the smoke now, and all of it, the field, the gate, already feels like something I read about someone else.
Elara: It happened to you. And to us, so don't go giving it away. Keep moving.
=> village

# The village meeting (fragment_one.dlg, C1-S11). Each branch is short on purpose.
~ village
do pause 2.0
[if ch1_oakhaven_warned_villagers] => village_warned
[if ch1_oakhaven_warned_leaders] => village_leaders
[if ch1_oakhaven_left_quietly] => village_quiet
=> village_none

~ village_warned
Kaelen: I told Mara I'd find out about the wells. I said a day. I should've said two.
Elara: She'll have every kettle in the lane boiling till you come back. Half of them won't know why, and all of them will complain.
Kaelen: Then I need an answer worth all that firewood.
=> under

~ village_leaders
Kaelen: Bran and Mara know. Tobb will, once Bran wakes him up and hands it to him in writing.
Kaelen: Three people. I don't even know how many live there. Was three enough?
Elara: Ask me after the council's met. Bran will have it all in ink by then, who said what and who sulked.
=> under

# Elara answers him sideways. She doesn't use his name here, and that's on purpose.
~ village_quiet
Kaelen: You think I should've told them. You've been quiet about it for a mile.
Elara: Tull and Wenna will be arguing about the water again by morning. Nobody's told them it was never the sluice.
=> under

~ village_none
Kaelen (Internal): Nobody back there knows what's under their village. I've stood in it, and I couldn't draw it for them.
=> under

# What Kaelen knows by the end of Chapter 1: the shrine words, and one memory of
# arguing for seven signatures (fragment_one.dlg). Nothing more. No Human Patch yet.
~ under
Kaelen: The words on the shrine wall. I knew them before my eyes got to the end of the line.
Elara: I remember. You went the colour of skimmed milk.
Kaelen: Nothing down there changes without seven signatures. Someone wrote that rule, and I remember arguing for it.
Kaelen: If any of what's under Oakhaven is mine, I want to know which parts before I put my hands on anything else.
Elara: Mara's bread is still Mara's bread, whoever laid the stones under her oven.
Elara: And if this turns into you owing the world something, don't you dare start paying it off on my arm.
=> onward

~ onward
Kaelen: I wasn't going to. It's your arm.
Elara: Come on, Kaelen. It's further than it looks, the wind's turning, and I'd like walls round us by morning.
Kaelen: Okay. Walls first. Then the list of names.
=> END
